-- 오병근 교수 회신 반영 (2026-11-18, 한글 파일). 받은 항목만 바꾸고 나머지 칸(직함·사진·전화 등)은 그대로 둔다. 여러 번 실행해도 결과가 같다.

update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 1995 공학사</li><li>서강대학교 1997 공학석사</li><li>서강대학교 2003 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>Northwestern University 박사후연구원 (2004–2006)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 조교수 (2006–2009)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 부교수 (2010–2014)</li><li>Auburn University 방문교수 (2012)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 교수 (2015–현재)</li><li>㈜앱클론 사외이사 (2017–2021)</li></ul><h3>주요 수상</h3><ul><li>제26회 대주산학연협력상 (2026)</li><li>한국공업화학회 공로상 (2024)</li></ul><h3>학회 활동</h3><ul><li>한국공업화학회 산학연협력 이사·위원장 (2021–2024)</li><li>한국바이오칩학회 이사·감사·부회장 (2006–현재)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Myeong-Jun Lee, Jeong-Hyeop Shin, Seung-Hun Jung, Ha Rim Ahn, Young Jo Kim, Jeong-Woo Choi, Jin-Ha Choi*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Single-tube total analysis system for ratiometric detection of exosomal miRNAs in breast cancer diagnosis," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 529, 173140 (2026)</li><li>Tae-Hwan Kim, Jang-Seob Lee, Jinwon Lee, Yong Hwan Kim, Jeong-Geol Na*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Intercellular whole-cell cascade strategy for robust CO-to-formate bioconversion," <em>Bioresource Technology</em> 460, 135310 (2026)</li><li>Myeong-Jun Lee, Jeong-Hyeop Shin, Seung-Hun Jung, Jeong-Woo Choi, Ha Rim Ahn, Jin-Ha Choi*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Hourglass-inspired total analysis system for the sensitive colorimetric detection of exosomal miRNA using the CRISPR-Cas12a system with isothermal amplification," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 512, 162729 (2025)</li><li>Tae-Hwan Kim, Jang-Seob Lee, Myeong-Jun Lee, Jinwon Lee, Young-Kee Kim, Jeong-Geol Na*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Two-stage Continuous CO Fermentation Process Strategy for High-titer Bioethanol Production Using <em>Clostridium autoethanogenum</em>," <em>Bioresource Technology</em> 132152 (2025)</li><li>Tae-Hwan Kim, Jiung Yun, Jang-Seob Lee, Myeong-Jun Lee, Jung Kye Kim, Jinwon Lee, Yong Hwan Kim, Jeong-Geol Na*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Enhancing Biological CO to Formate Conversion: Application of Aerophobic Coatings to Mitigate Bubble Coalescence," <em>ACS Sustainable Chemistry &amp; Engineering</em> 13(12), 4897–4907 (2025)</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Sogang University (1995)</li><li>M.S., Sogang University (1997)</li><li>Ph.D., Sogang University (2003)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Postdoctoral Fellow, Northwestern University (2004–2006)</li><li>Assistant Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2006–2009)</li><li>Associate Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2010–2014)</li><li>Visiting Professor, Auburn University (2012)</li><li>Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2015–present)</li><li>Outside Director, AbClon Inc. (2017–2021)</li></ul><h3>Selected Awards</h3><ul><li>The 26th Daeju Industry–Academia–Research Cooperation Award (2026)</li><li>Distinguished Service Award, Korean Society of Industrial and Engineering Chemistry (2024)</li></ul><h3>Professional Service</h3><ul><li>Director and Chair of Industry–Academia–Research Cooperation, Korean Society of Industrial and Engineering Chemistry (2021–2024)</li><li>Director, Auditor and Vice President, Korean BioChip Society (2006–present)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Myeong-Jun Lee, Jeong-Hyeop Shin, Seung-Hun Jung, Ha Rim Ahn, Young Jo Kim, Jeong-Woo Choi, Jin-Ha Choi*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Single-tube total analysis system for ratiometric detection of exosomal miRNAs in breast cancer diagnosis," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 529, 173140 (2026)</li><li>Tae-Hwan Kim, Jang-Seob Lee, Jinwon Lee, Yong Hwan Kim, Jeong-Geol Na*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Intercellular whole-cell cascade strategy for robust CO-to-formate bioconversion," <em>Bioresource Technology</em> 460, 135310 (2026)</li><li>Myeong-Jun Lee, Jeong-Hyeop Shin, Seung-Hun Jung, Jeong-Woo Choi, Ha Rim Ahn, Jin-Ha Choi*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Hourglass-inspired total analysis system for the sensitive colorimetric detection of exosomal miRNA using the CRISPR-Cas12a system with isothermal amplification," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 512, 162729 (2025)</li><li>Tae-Hwan Kim, Jang-Seob Lee, Myeong-Jun Lee, Jinwon Lee, Young-Kee Kim, Jeong-Geol Na*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Two-stage Continuous CO Fermentation Process Strategy for High-titer Bioethanol Production Using <em>Clostridium autoethanogenum</em>," <em>Bioresource Technology</em> 132152 (2025)</li><li>Tae-Hwan Kim, Jiung Yun, Jang-Seob Lee, Myeong-Jun Lee, Jung Kye Kim, Jinwon Lee, Yong Hwan Kim, Jeong-Geol Na*, Byung-Keun Oh*, "Enhancing Biological CO to Formate Conversion: Application of Aerophobic Coatings to Mitigate Bubble Coalescence," <em>ACS Sustainable Chemistry &amp; Engineering</em> 13(12), 4897–4907 (2025)</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>나노바이오 기술은 미세한 질병 마커를 검출하는 생체 센서부터 기후 위기 극복을 위한 친환경 탄소 전환 공정까지 우리 삶의 다양한 영역에 맞닿아 있습니다. 저희 연구실은 나노소재와 미세유체, 그리고 생체 촉매의 융합적 현상을 깊이 이해하고, 이를 의료 현장의 혁신적인 진단 기기와 지속 가능한 바이오 리파이너리(Biorefinery) 플랫폼으로 옮기는 연구를 합니다.</p><p>현장진단(POCT)을 위한 바이오센서 플랫폼 기술<br>미세유체기술 기반의 바이오센서 플랫폼은 복잡한 분석 장치들을 하나의 칩 위에 담아낸 작고 간편한 진단 기기입니다. 이를 통해 환자 진료 현장이나 환경 시료 채취 현장에서 즉각적인 검사가 가능해져, 신속하고 정확한 결과로 의료 서비스의 질을 획기적으로 높일 수 있습니다. 저희 연구실은 혁신적인 미세유체 제어 기술을 바탕으로, 현장에서 즉시 활용 가능한 초고감도 신속 항원 및 분자 진단 기기의 원천 플랫폼 기술을 개발합니다.</p><p>기능성 나노바이오 소재<br>최근 다양한 기능성을 융합한 생체적합성 나노입자가 차세대 핵심 소재로 큰 주목을 받고 있습니다. 나노바이오 소재는 물리화학적 특성을 세밀하게 제어할 수 있어 생명공학 분야 응용에 매우 적합합니다. 저희 연구실은 환경 모니터링 및 의료 바이오센싱 등 다양한 응용을 위해 새로운 나노구조 소재를 설계하고 합성하며, 이를 초고감도 바이오센서 플랫폼에 접목하여 진단 성능을 극대화하는 데 집중합니다.</p><p>생물학적 탄소 활용(Bio-CCU)<br>최근 온실가스를 감축하면서도 유용한 자원으로 재활용하는 탄소 활용기술(CCU)이 탄소중립 실현의 핵심으로 자리 잡고 있습니다. 특히 효소나 미생물 등 생체 시스템을 이용하는 생물학적 전환 방식은 매우 친환경적이고 지속 가능한 장점이 있습니다. 저희 연구실은 이산화탄소나 일산화탄소 같은 C1 가스를 고부가가치 화학물질로 전환하기 위해, 나노바이오 소재 기술과 우수한 생체 촉매(효소)를 융합한 고효율 친환경 바이오 리파이너리 공정을 설계하고 최적화하는 연구를 수행합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Nanobiotechnology reaches into many areas of daily life, from biosensors that detect trace disease markers to green carbon-conversion processes that address the climate crisis. Our laboratory seeks a deep understanding of the phenomena that arise where nanomaterials, microfluidics, and biocatalysts meet, and translates it into innovative diagnostic devices for clinical settings and sustainable biorefinery platforms.</p><p>Biosensor Platform Technology for Point-of-Care Testing (POCT)<br>A microfluidics-based biosensor platform is a compact, easy-to-use diagnostic device that integrates complex analytical instrumentation on a single chip. It enables immediate testing at the point of patient care or at environmental sampling sites, and its rapid, accurate results can markedly improve the quality of healthcare. Building on innovative microfluidic control technologies, our laboratory develops core platform technologies for ultrasensitive rapid antigen and molecular diagnostic devices that can be used on site.</p><p>Functional Nano-Bio Materials<br>Biocompatible nanoparticles that combine multiple functions are attracting great attention as key next-generation materials. Because their physicochemical properties can be finely tuned, nano-biomaterials are well suited to biotechnology applications. Our laboratory designs and synthesizes new nanostructured materials for applications including environmental monitoring and medical biosensing, and integrates them into ultrasensitive biosensor platforms to maximize diagnostic performance.</p><p>Biological Carbon Capture and Utilization (Bio-CCU)<br>Carbon capture and utilization (CCU), which cuts greenhouse gas emissions while recycling carbon into useful resources, has become central to achieving carbon neutrality. Biological conversion using enzymes and microorganisms is especially attractive for being environmentally benign and sustainable. To convert C1 gases such as carbon dioxide and carbon monoxide into high-value chemicals, our laboratory designs and optimizes efficient, green biorefinery processes that combine nano-bio materials technology with high-performance biocatalysts (enzymes).</p>$q$,
  lab_ko = $q$나노생명공학 연구실$q$,
  lab_en = $q$Nanobiotech Lab$q$,
  lab_url = $q$http://nanobiotech.sogang.ac.kr$q$,
  building = $q$R$q$,
  room = $q$505$q$,
  office = $q$리치과학관(R) 505호$q$,
  keywords = $q$Biosensor Platform, Point-of-Care Diagnostics, Nano-bio Materials, Bio-CCU$q$
where name_ko = '오병근';

select name_ko, title_ko, lab_ko, lab_url, office, keywords, length(bio_ko) bio_ko, length(bio_en) bio_en, length(research_ko) res_ko, length(research_en) res_en from faculty where name_ko = '오병근';
